  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional support for the private-non-for profit (PNFP) health sub-sector to promote universal health coverage in Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support the implementation of some of the key-reforms of the national BTVET strategy, both on a national/central level, and on the local level, in 4 districts in Western Uganda. It will support and strengthen policy formulation and implementation, it will assist in developing financing instruments and new modalities for training delivery, and it will support a restricted number of training providers in Kasese, Fort Portal, Hoima and Masindi. The project will strive for a close collaboration with Business Membership Organisations and private sector companies on all levels of intervention.</narrative>
  </description>
